notes               = "Untitled in source. بَرَبَط is the barbat, the Persian short-necked lute and ancestor of the oud; تیهو the see-see partridge, as in never-sated (page 155). Five lines: three ways of apprehending the beloved, then two questions that give up. Bare year ۱۳۷۵ → +621 = 1996. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

می‌شود تو را...
مثل بَرَبَطی نواخت... مثلِ تیهوئی شنید...
مثل آهویی شناخت...
در کدام آسمان پرواز...
در کدامین رود شنا می‌کنی...
۱۳۷۵

===machine===

You can be...
played like a barbat... heard like a partridge...
known like a gazelle...
In which sky do you fly...
in which river do you swim...
1375

===lantern===

You can be played like a barbat,
heard like a partridge,
known like a gazelle.
In which sky do you fly?
In which river do you swim?

1375

